Explaining cervical effacement and dilation is made easy with this 47-cm x 81-cm model with Spanish subtitles. Includes 10 lifelike models of the cervix that represent dilation from 1 cm to 10 cm. Also features colourful artwork that illustrates pelvic station and the baby’s positioning in the birth canal. Comes with carrying case. An easily portable tool for childbirth education.
\n
\n&nbsp;
\n
\n&nbsp;
\n
\nIn this 3-D display, 10 lifelike models of the cervix represent dilation from 1 cm to 10 cm. Colourful background art illustrates pelvic station and the baby’s positioning in the birth canal. Includes English text with Spanish subtitles. Comes with carrying case. 47 cm x 81 cm.
\n
\n&nbsp;

The EarScope Basic Wireless (MEDLW3E) is a compact and safe solution to look at the ear. The cap is detachable for hygienical reasons. The MEDLW3E has a 640x480 resolution and magnification of 20 ~ 30x. This model is delivered with disposable specula of 3, 4 and 5 mm (10 each).
\n
\n&nbsp;

The EarScope Pro Wireless (MEDLW4E) is a compact and safe solution for watching the eardrum and the external ear. The MEDL4E is the Pro model with 1,3 Megapixel resolution and a magnification of 55 ~ 90x. This model is delivered with disposable specula of 3, 4 and 5 mm (10 each).
\n
\n&nbsp;

Great for group or one-on-one instruction, this sturdy, life-size, standing display shows the childbearing cycle through 6 weeks post-partum, including an image of the involution of the uterus after birth. Images are overlapping and grow as a baby develops throughout pregnancy. Also covers making healthy choices and knowing when you are in labor. The back of the display features a timeline of pregnancy. Perfect for explaining each stage of foetal development.
\n
\n&nbsp;

The IriScope Wireless (MEDLW4R) offers a new, fast and easy way to make pictures of eyes. The IriScope Wireless has 2x2 LED's (white/yellow) that illuminate the side of the eye which reduces the reflections in the image as well as the discomfort by bright light. The yellow LED's provide better images of dark irises. The images have a maximum resolution of 1.3 Megapixel.
\n
\n&nbsp;

The CapillaryScope 500 (MEDL4N5) is a special version intended for looking at the microcirculation (microcapillar function) under nails. It is very easy to capture and store highly detailed magnified images. The magnification rate is 500x.
\n
\n&nbsp;

Designed to make a lasting impression, this display features semi-clear wombs that hold models of babies at 10-, 12-, 14-, and 16-weeks gestation. The halves of the wombs can be separated to allow viewers to handle the foetus models, which have a realistic feel and weight. 47 cm x 24 cm x 20 cm.
